WEBVTT

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.056
Plus, on top of his credentials,

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.586
Mohamed proved his competence
in reading a room

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:06.806
with that joke about
the front row being his shield.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.606
If you haven't already demonstrated

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.056
that you're capable, though,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.396
showing vulnerability can have
the opposite effect.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:16.926
Take a recent study
of lawyers interviewing for jobs.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.156
Focusing on expressing themselves

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.751
only increased their odds
of getting a job offer

00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:25.226
if their resumes had already
impressed the interviewer.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.916
The only lawyers who benefited
from being authentic

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:31.139
were the ones who'd been ranked
in the top 10 percent of candidates